  "description": "ZEZVAF crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C106 H112 Gd8 N12 O40,2(C2 H6 O1),2(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.572-3.931 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.28-112.34°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C112H128Cl4Gd8N12O42. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
